# Getting Started (Windows, from scratch)

## Built With

- **Python 3.12** (tested on 3.12.10)
- **PyTorch** (CUDA build, matched to your GPU)
- **NVIDIA NeMo** (`nemo_toolkit` — provides access to the Canary and Parakeet models)
- **customtkinter** (GUI)
- **FFmpeg** (decodes non-WAV audio files such as MP3/M4A/FLAC/OGG)

<sub>[(back to top)](#getting-started-windows-from-scratch)</sub>

## Prerequisites

- **Windows 10 or 11.**
- **An NVIDIA GPU.** Only NVIDIA cards have been tested (3070, 3090, 5070 Ti, 5090).
  - **Canary** (higher accuracy): needs **12+ GB VRAM** (e.g. RTX 3090 24 GB, RTX 5070 Ti 16 GB).
  - **Parakeet** (faster): works on **< 12 GB VRAM** (e.g. RTX 3070 8 GB).
- **Disk space + internet for the models.** The models are downloaded automatically from Hugging Face the first time you select one (Parakeet ≈ 1–2 GB, Canary ≈ several GB) and cached under `%USERPROFILE%\.cache\huggingface`. The first launch with a given model is slow; later launches are fast.
- A current **NVIDIA GPU driver** (update from the NVIDIA app / GeForce Experience if unsure).

